}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 3\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $v + 3=0.$" 13194139535794 17592186045443 true] [17592186528094 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528101 13194139535794 17592186045443 true] [17592186528094 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535794 17592186045443 true] [17592186528094 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 4\\right)^{2} \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139535794 17592186045443 true] [17592186528094 1072 #uuid "5623f019-5b29-5f61-95d8-7be3055bcc58" 13194139535794 17592186045443 true] [17592186528094 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\left(u + 4\\right)^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2 u + 8 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 8)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 8)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(u + 4\\right).\\e